# rule poly.6 space(gate, tap_abutting_diff) >= 300nm
# rule hvntm.6b space(ptap_butting_edge, hvntm) >= 0nm

# --- Left out ---
# Not expressible yet: difftap.2/2b (channel width, 0.42/0.36um: needs W, not
# width), difftap.4/5/16 (tap bound by diffusion), poly.10/11 (corner and turn
# rules), poly.13 (gate length inside hvi, 0.5um: needs L, not width),
# lvtn.3b (S/D direction spacing), lvtn.10 (enclosure excluding coincident
# edges), npc.5 (maximum enclosure), licon.2b/2c/2d (slotted-licon spacing by
# edge length), rpm.1b-1f (exact resistor widths), varac.2/6 (tap-width and
# varactor-tap spacing), hv.* and vhvi.* (net propagation of high voltage),
# m1.pd.1-m4.pd.1 and x.18 (recommended only; pd.1's "oxide pattern density"
# is not a metal density this deck can state with certainty), m1.X.1 (waffle
# windows), pwres.*, photo.*, tunm.*, denmos.*, depmos.*, extd.*, uhvi.*,
# vpp.*, mf.*, rdl.*, indm.*, x.12-x.29 (frame, seal ring and cell-name rules).
# N/A in [S1] and absent from [S3]: capm.2b/5/6/8/10/12 as [S1] numbers them
#   ([S3] gives capm.2b as a bottom-plate spacing of 1.2um that needs same-net
#   selection; capm.5 0.14um is via3 to capm, which conflicts with capm.4 over
#   the plate, so it waits on a clearer source).
# Devices: diodes (pw2nd, pd2nw), bipolars (npn, pnp), the native nfets
#   (03v3_nvt, 05v0_nvt, areaid.le) and the 20V devices need the well or
#   substrate as a net, which this deck does not connect; VPP capacitors are
#   fixed cells with no marker a recogniser can use. MOS bulk terminals are left
#   off for the same reason, so well_bias has nothing to examine and is not
#   configured.
# Latch-up: esd_latchup needs a guard-ring width and tap distance that [S1]
#   does not state.
